    "tiger_m_client": "The Young Tiger, Lomé",
    "tiger_m_tools": "React, TypeScript, Tauri, PocketBase, Hostinger VPS",
    "tiger_m_status": "In production since September 2026",
    "tiger_s_context": "<p>The Young Tiger distributes farming machinery and generators in Lomé: three shops, one warehouse and around ten distributors. When I started working with them in February 2026, everything was handled by hand. I first set up their PCs and a first management tool on Google Sheets.</p>",
    "tiger_s_problem": "<p>With three shops, a warehouse and distributors taking stock to resell, the spreadsheet could no longer keep up. The owner wanted to know at any moment what sells, where the stock is and who owes what, without being on site.</p>",
    "tiger_s_solution": "<p>The spreadsheet quickly hit its limits. So I scoped, built and deployed a real management app myself:</p><ul><li><strong>Three roles, three interfaces</strong>: the seller cashes in and prints the invoice, the manager runs all three shops, the owner follows everything from his phone.</li><li><strong>Sales and credit</strong>: the amount received decides whether a sale is cash or credit, the debt opens on its own and is paid off instalment by instalment, with a receipt each time.</li><li><strong>Inventory and warehouse</strong>: stock arrivals, transfers from the warehouse to the shops, low stock alerts, no way to sell more than what exists.</li><li><strong>Distributors</strong>: stock held and debt of each distributor calculated live.</li><li><strong>Documents</strong>: invoices, quotes, receipts and delivery notes in A5 duplicate, based on the template the client already used.</li><li><strong>Go-live</strong>: VPS server, domain name, app installed on the shop PCs and on the owner's phone.</li></ul>",
    "tiger_s_results": "<ul><li>App in production since September 2026, used daily by the owner, 2 managers and 3 sellers</li><li>Three shops, a warehouse and around ten distributors connected in a single tool</li><li>More than 200 products in the catalogue</li><li>The owner tracks sales, stock and credit remotely</li><li>Four types of printed documents generated automatically</li></ul>",
    "tiger_s_learned": "<p>The hardest part was not the code but understanding how this business really works: distributors, credit, sales paid in several instalments. I learned to break a big project into stages, get each one approved by the client and handle a real production launch.</p>",
    "tiger_k1": "Shops",
    "tiger_k2": "Warehouse",
    "tiger_k3": "Distributors tracked",
    "tiger_k4": "Products in catalogue",
    "erp_m_year": "2026",
    "erp_m_role": "Designer & developer",
    "erp_m_type": "Commercial product",
    "erp_m_client": "Amirson Machine, Atakpamé",
    "erp_m_tools": "Python, SQLite, Supabase, Google Apps Script",
    "erp_m_status": "V2 running since July 2026",
    "erp_s_context": "<p>Many shop owners in Lomé still track stock and invoices on paper or in a makeshift Excel file. Alpha ERP was built for them: a simple, affordable tool that keeps running when the internet drops.</p>",
    "erp_s_problem": "<p>Amirson Machine sells machines in Atakpamé while the owner lives in Lomé. He wanted to follow his business remotely. A first step, a read-only dashboard synced from V1, confirmed the need. But the owner wanted more than a view: a real connected app he could use from his phone.</p>",
    "erp_s_solution": "<p>Alpha now comes in three tiers:</p><ul><li><strong>Google Sheets ERP</strong> (entry level): automated invoicing with Apps Script, one click invoices, sales and customer credit tracking.</li><li><strong>Alpha ERP V1</strong> (desktop software): a Windows app in Python with a local SQLite database. Inventory, sales, credit, PDF invoices (A4, A5, 80 mm receipt), daily cash closing and machine-bound licence key.</li><li><strong>Alpha ERP V2</strong> (web): two apps connected to the same Supabase database. The seller app, on the shop PC, opens straight on “New sale”. The owner app, installed on his phone, shows a dashboard with charts, exports invoices as PDF, sends them over WhatsApp and exports data to Excel.</li></ul>",
    "erp_s_results": "<ul><li>V2 installed at Amirson Machine in July 2026</li><li>The owner follows his sales from Lomé, in real time</li><li>Sales by unit or by the metre, three invoice formats</li><li>Adapted for Amirson Quincaillerie, with sales by the metre, the litre and the roll</li></ul>",
    "erp_s_learned": "<p>Moving from V1 to V2 taught me when to start over. Rather than patching more than 10,000 lines of Python, I rebuilt the tool for the web while keeping the same data model, and the installation landed on time.</p>",
