    "data_m_client": "ASSAFETO (Togo Midwives Association)",
    "data_m_tools": "Google Forms, Google Sheets, Drive",
    "data_m_status": "Delivered",
    "data_s_context": "<p>ASSAFETO wanted, for the first time, a digital database of all its members across the country. No central register existed: depending on the region, data was scattered, incomplete or missing.</p><p>The database had to help manage members, improve internal communication and give the association a reliable reference file.</p>",
    "data_s_problem": "<p>How do you collect and clean more than 1,900 answers from all over Togo, typed by people not used to digital tools and shared through WhatsApp groups, and deliver a clean file sorted by region?</p>",
    "data_s_solution": "<p>A three step process:</p><ul><li><strong>Collection</strong>: a structured Google Form (identity, region, entry and exit dates), shared in the association's regional WhatsApp groups.</li><li><strong>Cleaning</strong>: removing duplicates (sometimes the same person four times), fixing typing errors, standardising formats with advanced Google Sheets formulas.</li><li><strong>Validation</strong>: lists sent to each regional lead for review, then their corrections merged in.</li></ul>",
    "data_s_results": "<ul><li>1,900+ answers collected, reduced to 1,400+ real members</li><li>The association's first centralised digital database</li><li>Data sorted by region for local management</li><li>A clean file usable from day one, plus one PDF per region</li></ul>",
    "data_s_learned": "<p>The real difficulty in data cleaning is not technical, it is human: you have to anticipate the mistakes of hundreds of people without losing useful information. I also learned to explain things simply, gather feedback and deliver a reliable result from very raw data.</p>",
