    "proj_barber_cat": "Side project · Web app",
    "proj_barber_title": "Biloumbil Barber",
    "proj_barber_desc": "Online booking, a flexible schedule and loyalty for a barbershop in Lomé. A no-account client app and a barber dashboard, built for the phone.",
    "barber_m_year": "2026",
    "barber_m_role": "Design and development",
    "barber_m_type": "Side project",
    "barber_m_client": "Barbershop (demo)",
    "barber_m_tools": "React, Vite, Supabase, Vitest, Netlify",
    "barber_m_status": "Live demo",
    "barber_s_context": "<p>In Lomé, booking a barber still happens over the phone or on WhatsApp. The barber answers between two cuts, forgets to write it down, and two clients show up at the same time. I wanted a tool for <strong>a single shop</strong>, not yet another marketplace: the app carries the shop's name and doubles as its marketing tool.</p>",
    "barber_s_problem": "<p>How do you let clients book on their own, with no account or password, while the barber stays in control of his schedule, and without two people ever getting the same slot?</p>",
    "barber_s_solution": "<p>Two apps in one project:</p><ul><li><strong>The client app</strong>, installable on the phone: pick a service, see the slots that are really free, apply a promo code, then follow bookings, points and vouchers.</li><li><strong>The barber dashboard</strong>, on computer and phone: requests arrive live, he accepts, declines or <strong>suggests another time</strong>, and each action prepares a ready-made WhatsApp message.</li><li><strong>The phone number as a loyalty card</strong>: every way of writing it (“90 11 22 33”, “+228 90112233”…) is normalised so one client stays one client.</li><li><strong>Points you can't game</strong>: they are credited when the barber marks the client as present, and a personal voucher is created automatically at the threshold.</li><li><strong>Built-in marketing</strong>: promotions on the home screen, promo codes open to all or tied to one number, and a list of clients who haven't come back in six weeks.</li></ul>",
    "barber_s_results": "<ul><li>Two complete apps: 8 client screens, 12 barber screens</li><li>Passwordless yet secure: a secret token per phone, no direct table access</li><li>Every booking rechecked in the database (hours, overlaps, price, promo code) by PostgreSQL functions</li><li>Business logic covered by unit tests (Vitest)</li><li>A full demo mode that runs in the browser, with no server</li></ul>",
    "barber_s_learned": "<p>The most interesting part wasn't the interface but the business rules: what is a free slot when there's a break, a pending request and an open proposal? Who can see what without an account? Writing those rules once, testing them, then having the database enforce them is what makes the tool reliable.</p>",
