    "ytv_m_status": "Website live and indexed on Google, 7 videos ready",
    "ytv_s_context": "<p>When I started with The Young Tiger, the brand had <strong>no online presence at all</strong>: no logo, no brand guidelines, no Google listing, no social accounts, no website. A customer looking for a generator in Lomé simply couldn't find them. I built everything from scratch.</p>",
    "ytv_s_problem": "<p>How do you make a brand findable and make people want to get in touch, no prices shown, and customers browsing on 3G phones? The common thread: every touchpoint, Google, social and website, leads to a WhatsApp conversation with a seller.</p>",
    "ytv_s_solution": "<p>Everything, from the brand to the videos:</p><ul><li><strong>Visual identity</strong>: the logo, the brand guidelines (white first, orange accents), posters and print material.</li><li><strong>Google</strong>: created the Google Business listings for each shop, with the pin on the storefront, opening hours and a link to the website, then submitted the site to Search Console with a sitemap and business details Google can read.</li><li><strong>Social</strong>: created the Facebook, Instagram and TikTok accounts, wrote the bios, connected everything in Meta Business Suite. WhatsApp Business set up with a greeting, an away message and quick replies, including one with the Maps link of each shop.</li><li><strong>The showcase website</strong>: the tagline “When the power goes out, the tiger wakes up”, four use cases (home, shop, field, worksite), a 200+ product catalogue pulled from the management software, galleries for products shot from several angles, and a WhatsApp button with a pre-written message on every product.</li><li><strong>Videos</strong>: I produce them myself, 7 so far. Motion videos built from animated text (“The tiger wakes up”, “Is your business stopping?”, “How much power for my home?”, “Power cut”), before / after videos edited with royalty-free footage (“Is your field wearing you out?”, “From paddy to white rice”) and a “New arrivals” video edited with real factory footage sent by the client. Every video ends on the same end screen, in 9:16 and 4:5.</li><li><strong>Posts</strong>: an “Our shops” carousel, 31 cut-out product photos for the team's posters, ready-to-paste captions and a launch calendar of 10 posts.</li></ul>",
    "ytv_s_results": "<ul><li>A brand that started from zero and now exists everywhere: Google, Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, WhatsApp Business and a website</li><li>The website shows up on Google for “The Young Tiger Lomé”, right under the shops' Maps listings, with both pages indexed</li><li>200+ products online and 3 shops on Google Maps, with directions</li><li>Google PageSpeed score of 100 for performance, accessibility and SEO, on mobile and desktop</li><li>7 videos ready to post, all sharing the same end screen</li></ul>",
    "ytv_s_learned": "<p>Building a brand from scratch is mostly about holding the same choices everywhere, from the logo to the videos. Show options rather than ask for opinions: three versions of the end screen settled in one message a colour question that had dragged on for days. The client's own footage, his rice huller running or his machines at the factory, builds more trust than any stock video.</p>",
